e II cannot be modeled as a discrete uniform distribution. Each outcome is not equally likely, as there are likely to be more children than adults in the school.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>Random variable III cannot be modeled as a discrete uniform distribution. This is because the height of a basketball player is a real number, so the support is not finite. Moreover, each outcome is not equally likely.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Therefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"</p>\n</div></div>",
